FUNDAMENTALS
- Hardware Root of Trust never leaves silicon
- Dual independent signatures required for any firmware change
- Continuous runtime measurement + remote attestation
- Network isolation + signed actuator commands
- Tamper event = immediate key zeroization + safe-mode lockout

KEY COMPONENTS / TYPES
SecureElement      : Tamper-resistant chip (ST-SAFE / Infineon SLE 78)
                     Stores device-unique RSA-4096 or ECC-P-384 private key
                     + X.509 certificates. Keys never exported.

TEE                : ARM TrustZone or CryptoCell
                     Runs measured-boot event log (MBEL)
                     Signs hashes of kernel, ROS 2, NVIDIA Isaac, AI models
                     every few seconds with attestation key.

OTA Payload        : Dual-signed container
                     1. Manufacturer HSM signature
                     2. Owner vault signature (MFA + home HSM)
                     Missing or invalid signature = reject + immutable log.

ActuatorCommand    : Per-device signed instruction
                     Validated by motion controller + policy engine
                     (force limits, time-of-day, etc.) before execution.

VLAN / mTLS        : Dedicated segment, certificate pinning,
                     no inbound internet, egress only HTTPS:443 + SNI check.

TamperSensor       : Chassis pressure / GPIO / debug-port monitor
                     Trigger = zeroize all private keys + disable actuators.

VARIABLES / STATE
device_unique_key  : Stored only inside SecureElement
attestation_hash   : Rolling measurement of loaded images
owner_signature    : Generated on home hub after MFA
known_good_baseline: Stored in secure ledger for remote verification
quarantine_flag    : Set on any attestation deviation
safe_mode          : Actuators locked, network isolated, keys erased

